import ../../../ui/source_edits.dl

to get [an edit from row] {integer:row} [column] {integer:first} [through] {integer:last} [inserting] {string:text}:
    return a JSON object containing [JSON child "range" is (an LSP range from line row and character first to line row and character last), JSON text "newText" is text]

set document to a UI source document named "game.dl" at "file:///workspace/game.dl" prefixed by "# hidden\n" containing "😀 alpha\nbeta" using UI CPU analysis
set original to document's source
set edits to a JSON array containing [an edit from row 2 column 0 through 4 inserting "B", an edit from row 1 column 3 through 8 inserting "A"]
set change to a UI source change for document applying edits with caret 15
free edits
require condition ((change's succeeded) and (change's text = "😀 A\nB")) reporting "Unordered source edits did not use original UTF-16 coordinates."
require condition (change's caret = 8) reporting "The caret did not follow multiple edits."
require condition (document's source = original) reporting "Preparing an edit mutated the source before acceptance."
require condition (change is current for UI source document document) reporting "A newly prepared edit was already stale."

set edits to a JSON array containing [an edit from row 1 column 3 through 8 inserting "A", an edit from row 0 column 0 through 8 inserting "hidden replacement"]
set rejected to a UI source change for document applying edits with caret 15
free edits
require condition ((rejected's succeeded = false) and (rejected's text = original)) reporting "An edit of hidden context partially changed the visible source."
require condition (rejected's reason = "This edit changes protected project context.") reporting "A protected edit did not explain why it cannot be applied."

set crossing to a JSON object containing [JSON child "range" is (an LSP range from line 0 and character 0 to line 1 and character 3), JSON text "newText" is "crossing"]
set edits to a JSON array containing [crossing]
set rejected to a UI source change for document applying edits with caret 15
free edits
require condition (rejected's succeeded = false) reporting "An edit crossing the prefix was silently clamped."

set edits to a JSON array containing [an edit from row 1 column 3 through 8 inserting "A", an edit from row 1 column 4 through 6 inserting "overlap"]
set rejected to a UI source change for document applying edits with caret 15
free edits
require condition ((rejected's succeeded = false) and (rejected's text = original)) reporting "Overlapping edits were partially applied."

set edits to a JSON array containing [an edit from row 1 column 3 through 3 inserting "1", an edit from row 1 column 3 through 3 inserting "2"]
set inserted to a UI source change for document applying edits with caret 5
free edits
require condition ((inserted's succeeded) and (inserted's text = "😀 12alpha\nbeta")) reporting "Concurrent insertions lost their protocol order."
require condition (inserted's caret = 7) reporting "The caret did not follow concurrent insertions."

edit UI source document document to (the string form of "changed") at 1.0 seconds
require condition ((change is current for UI source document document) = false) reporting "A prepared edit remained valid after another change."
free UI source document document
print line "Source edits are atomic, Unicode-aware, ordered and protect hidden project context."
